                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_qLQ8VK": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p>The Games Cube's growth has been a story of evolution.<br/>What began with Lindsay and Alex doing everything themselves gradually became a business supported by a team of employees. The company grew its stock, its customer base and its ability to serve Magic players throughout Australia.<br/>And while the range expanded into other trading card games, board games, roleplaying games, miniatures and painting, Magic singles remained at the heart of the business. The company is still described as an Australian family-owned gaming business specialising in MTG and tabletop games. <br/>Today, The Games Cube's online singles operation offers cards across an enormous range of sets, formats, rarities and finishes. Its buylist allows players to sell cards for cash or receive a store-credit bonus, giving players another way to turn cards they no longer need into their next deck or collection.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
