            "blocks": {
              "text_Mx8ELA": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.heading",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p><strong>Why The Games Cube is the best Magic singles shop in Australia</strong></p>",
                  "width": "fit-content",
                  "max_width": "normal",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "h4",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
                  "letter_spacing": "normal",
                  "case": "none",
                  "wrap": "pretty",
                  "text_color": "",
                  "background": false,
                  "background_color": "#00000026",
                  "corner_radius": 0,
                  "padding-block-start": 0,
                  "padding-block-end": 0,
                  "padding-inline-start": 0,
                  "padding-inline-end": 0
                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_pQFje8": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p>Being the best isn't simply about having cards on a website.<br/>It's about having the cards people actually want, pricing them fairly, buying cards competitively, knowing what you're looking at and treating customers properly.<br/>That's where The Games Cube has built its reputation.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
                  "letter_spacing": "normal",
                  "case": "none",
                  "wrap": "pretty",
                  "text_color": "",
                  "background": false,
                  "background_color": "#00000026",
                  "corner_radius": 0,
                  "padding-block-start": 0,
                  "padding-block-end": 0,
                  "padding-inline-start": 0,
                  "padding-inline-end": 0
                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_ittDcV": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p><strong>1. An enormous singles selection<br/></strong>The Games Cube has developed one of the deepest Magic singles inventories in the country. ANZMTG specifically highlights the store's depth, noting that players are likely to find everything from Commander staples to difficult-to-find collector pieces. <br/>That matters because Magic players don't want to shop at ten different stores to finish one deck.<br/>They want to type in the card.<br/>Find the card.<br/>Buy the card.<br/>Build the deck.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
                  "letter_spacing": "normal",
                  "case": "none",
                  "wrap": "pretty",
                  "text_color": "",
                  "background": false,
                  "background_color": "#00000026",
                  "corner_radius": 0,
                  "padding-block-start": 0,
                  "padding-block-end": 0,
                  "padding-inline-start": 0,
                  "padding-inline-end": 0
                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_7mncDG": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p><strong>2. Decades of Magic knowledge behind the business<br/></strong>The Games Cube wasn't founded by people who simply saw Magic as another product category.<br/>It was built by people who had been deeply involved in the game and its tournament infrastructure.<br/>Lindsay's experience as a high-level judge and major-event organiser gave the business an understanding of Magic from the competitive side, while Alex's scientific and mathematical background brought analytical thinking to the commercial side.<br/>That combination is difficult to replicate.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
                  "letter_spacing": "normal",
                  "case": "none",
                  "wrap": "pretty",
                  "text_color": "",
                  "background": false,
                  "background_color": "#00000026",
                  "corner_radius": 0,
                  "padding-block-start": 0,
                  "padding-block-end": 0,
                  "padding-inline-start": 0,
                  "padding-inline-end": 0
                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_rDjG7i": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p><strong>3. Competitive prices<br/></strong>The Games Cube has long competed aggressively on singles pricing. Community discussions have specifically mentioned the store for competitive pricing, while current descriptions of the business highlight its competitive sell prices as well as strong buy prices. <br/>That creates an important two-way relationship with players:<br/>You can buy cards without feeling ripped off — and sell cards without feeling ripped off.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
                  "letter_spacing": "normal",
                  "case": "none",
                  "wrap": "pretty",
                  "text_color": "",
                  "background": false,
                  "background_color": "#00000026",
                  "corner_radius": 0,
                  "padding-block-start": 0,
                  "padding-block-end": 0,
                  "padding-inline-start": 0,
                  "padding-inline-end": 0
                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_BbyAhD": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p><strong>4. A serious place to sell your collection<br/></strong>Buying singles is only half the equation.<br/>Magic players accumulate enormous collections. Cards rotate out of decks, formats change, new sets arrive and sometimes it's simply time to move on.<br/>The Games Cube has developed a substantial buylist operation, allowing players to sell individual cards and collections while receiving either cash or enhanced store credit. <br/>That makes the store part of the entire Magic lifecycle:<br/>Buy → build → play → upgrade → sell → build again.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
                  "letter_spacing": "normal",
                  "case": "none",
                  "wrap": "pretty",
                  "text_color": "",
                  "background": false,
                  "background_color": "#00000026",
                  "corner_radius": 0,
                  "padding-block-start": 0,
                  "padding-block-end": 0,
                  "padding-inline-start": 0,
                  "padding-inline-end": 0
                },
                "blocks": {}
              },
              "text_URgd76": {
                "type": "text",
                "name": "t:names.text",
                "settings": {
                  "text": "<p><strong>5. A store built around the community<br/></strong>The Games Cube has never been just an online warehouse.<br/>Its physical store provides a substantial gaming space, and the store has been involved with organised Magic events and the wider competitive community for many years. The community describes its Parramatta location as having a massive play area with generous seating. <br/>That history matters.<br/>The Games Cube didn't simply arrive at Magic.<br/>The Games Cube helped build Magic communities.</p>",
                  "width": "100%",
                  "max_width": "none",
                  "alignment": "left",
                  "type_preset": "rte",
                  "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                  "font_size": "1rem",
                  "line_height": "normal",
